                <pb facs="0211" n="121" sameAs="frus:frus1918Russiav02/pg121"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 861.00/1617</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Russia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Francis</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Vologda</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1918-04-12T22:00:00+02:31"><hi rendition="#italic">April 12, 1918,
                                10 p.m.</hi></date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received April 19, 3.22 p.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>95. Your special No. 55 of April 9, 5 p.m. I made no statement that the landing
                    was with consent or by agreement of Allies. Same report published here. Emanated
                    from Moscow and I am endeavoring to ascertain the source. Transmitted to you my
                    verbatim statement in my No. 86, April 10, 4 p.m.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Francis</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
